Web Computer Modern / New Computer Modern fonts
-----------------------------------------------

The renderer includes 18 WebCM WOFF2 faces in src/renderer/assets/fonts/: the
10-point Sans, Serif, and Mono families at weights 400 (Regular), 500 (Book),
and 700 (Bold), each with its matching italic or oblique face. They load from
the application bundle only and are never fetched at run time. They are a
subset of the web-computer-modern package, a WOFF2 conversion of New Computer
Modern, which derives from Latin Modern:

  Package: web-computer-modern@1.1.0-new-cm-7-0-2
  https://www.npmjs.com/package/web-computer-modern
  Original typeface: New Computer Modern 7.0.2
  https://ctan.org/pkg/newcomputermodern
  Conversion: WebCM WOFF2 conversion, 2025-05-01

The published conversion manifest, MANIFEST-WebCM.txt, and the license text,
GUST-FONT-LICENSE.txt, sit beside the faces. The files keep their WebCM names,
because the GUST Font License requires the names assigned to the converted New
Computer Modern faces. The fonts are distributed under the GUST Font License
1.0 or later (LPPL 1.3c or later). The complete terms are reproduced at:

  licenses/GUST-FONT-LICENSE.txt

