Node, Electron, and Chromium
----------------------------

The Electron application includes the production Node package closure
recorded by package-lock.json and the pinned Electron runtime. It also
includes the npm packages that Vite inlines into the renderer bundle, such as
React and NiiVue (@niivue/niivue, BSD-2-Clause, the brain viewer), which the
renderer build records in out/renderer/bundled-packages.json. Each installer
includes a machine-readable distributable manifest and consolidated Node
package notices, with each package's license text, under
dependency-manifests/. NiiVue's license text comes from its upstream release
tag, because its npm package ships none. NiiVue embeds its default font atlas,
rendered from the Roboto typeface, and its matcap images. Electron's own
LICENSE and LICENSES.chromium.html stay in the application bundle, and package
validation requires both files.

The brain viewer reads FreeSurfer's fsaverage template files from the
operator's FreeSurfer installation at run time; Supraspina does not bundle
them.

